<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        The <strong>Execution Log</strong> under the rules shows every time a rule was triggered: the rule, the
        trigger event, when it ran and the result. Turn on <strong>Failures only</strong> to hide the rest.
    </FluentText>
    <ul>
        <li>A tick means every action worked.</li>
        <li>A failure means at least one action didn't. Open the entry to see which, and the error.</li>
        <li><strong>Skipped</strong> means the rule was triggered but a condition wasn't met, so no actions ran.
            Open the entry for <strong>Why it was skipped</strong>.</li>
    </ul>
    <HelpNote>
        Rule not doing anything? Check the engine switch and the rule's own Enabled switch are on, that the
        trigger client is the kiosk running the game, and look for Skipped entries in the log.
    </HelpNote>
    <FluentText>
        The <strong>Automation Rule Status</strong> dashboard widget shows a rule's state and last run, and lets
        Admins turn it on or off from a dashboard.
    </FluentText>
</HelpTab>
